WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:01.110
New term.

2
00:00:01.160 --> 00:00:02.800
A new friendship group.

3
00:00:02.850 --> 00:00:04.420
They share a habit.

4
00:00:04.470 --> 00:00:08.090
When they do it, they laugh,
and they get invited out.

5
00:00:08.140 --> 00:00:11.000
The newcomer watches, then copies.

6
00:00:11.050 --> 00:00:15.260
Each time, a little spark of
reward keeps the loop turning.

7
00:00:15.310 --> 00:00:18.640
If friends and rewards can
build an addiction like this,

8
00:00:18.690 --> 00:00:20.610
could learning undo it?

9
00:00:20.660 --> 00:00:24.150
In this mission, you'll see
how peer influence works:

10
00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:30.010
we observe and imitate friends, and seeing
them rewarded is vicarious reinforcement.

11
00:00:30.060 --> 00:00:34.210
You'll find out how rewards, like
a buzz or relief from stress,

12
00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:35.840
keep a habit going.

13
00:00:35.890 --> 00:00:39.660
And you'll test a big idea:
if something was learned,

14
00:00:39.710 --> 00:00:41.690
can new learning change it?

15
00:00:41.740 --> 00:00:46.760
Your mission: decide whether what friends
and rewards have built can be undone.
